#+TITLE: Windows COM backends ignore the explicit job DWG
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation
#+BRANCH: codex/alfe-com-job-drawing

* Evidence
SCHME !339 job 564204 ran ALFE 2.3.78 with a unique job DWG, but the emitted
BricsCAD bridge only used Documents.Add / ActiveDocument, never Documents.Open.
The historical suite then loaded its resources from the runner's Documents
folder. AutoCAD's COM emitter has the same omission. The emitted bridges and
native logs are retained by the SCHME qualification job.

* Implementation
Pass the requested DWG into both COM emitters, open it before plug-in startup
and activate it. No failed open may silently fall back to a blank drawing.
Unit emitter checks pass under SBCL; native validation is still required.
